        "original_id": "bb0d5f7c-c4dc-5bcf-831b-844aa579301b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Donaldson, André Cayatte\n- Roles: film director, producer, writer, filmmaker, lawyer\n- Films: The World's Fastest Indian, Smash Palace, No Way Out, Thirteen Days, Dante's Peak\n- Topics: crime, justice, moral responsibility\n\nFacts:\n- André Cayatte was born on 3 February 1909 in Carcassonne and died on 6 February 1989 in Paris.\n- André Cayatte was a French filmmaker and lawyer known for films about crime, justice, and moral responsibility.\n- Roger Donaldson was born on 15 November 1945 and is an Australian-born New Zealand film director, producer, and writer.\n- Roger Donaldson directed films including Smash Palace in 1981, No Way Out in 1987, Dante's Peak in 1997, Thirteen Days in 2000, and The World's Fastest Indian in 2005.\n- Roger Donaldson's United States-shot films included No Way Out and Thirteen Days, both starring Kevin Costner.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "938ece9c-330c-5bae-89b7-eaac1c0519a8",
        "text": "Page: Roger Donaldson. Sentence: Roger Donaldson (born 15 November 1945) is an Australian-born New Zealand film director, producer and writer whose films include \"The World's Fastest Indian\" (2005), acclaimed 1981 relationship drama \"Smash Palace\", and a run of titles shot in the United States, including the Kevin Costner films \"No Way Out\" (1987) and \"Thirteen Days\" (2000), and the 1997 disaster film \"Dante's Peak\".\nPage: André Cayatte. Sentence: André Cayatte (3 February 1909, Carcassonne – 6 February 1989, Paris) was a French filmmaker and lawyer, who became known for his films centering on themes of crime, justice, and moral responsibility.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
